BT /F2 19 Tf 101.9 694.2 Td (Choosing a Learning Rate: A Short Practical Note) Tj ET
BT /F3 11.5 Tf 226.2 672.5 Td (ML 201 course handout, Lecture 7) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.5 Tf 118.7 657.6 Td (Demo material for Clueless. The experiment and its numbers are illustrative, not published results.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 286.1 626.6 Td (Abstract) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 110.0 610.4 Td (The learning rate is the setting that most often decides whether gradient descent works at all. We) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 110.0 596.1 Td (train the same small classifier with five learning rates and report the final validation loss and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 110.0 581.8 Td (number of epochs needed to converge. A rate of 0.01 reaches the lowest loss, 0.27, in 14 epochs. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 110.0 567.5 Td (rate of 0.001 reaches a similar loss but needs 96 epochs, and a rate of 1.0 diverges within 3 epochs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 110.0 553.2 Td (We end with three rules that are easy to apply in practice.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 82.0 515.6 Td (1. Introduction) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 82.0 496.6 Td (Gradient descent updates the weights by moving against the gradient of the loss. The size of that) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 82.0 481.6 Td (move is the learning rate, written eta. If eta is too small, training is correct but slow. If it is too large,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 82.0 466.7 Td (each step overshoots the minimum and the loss grows instead of shrinking. Between the two there is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 82.0 451.7 Td (usually a wide range that works, and finding it takes only a few short runs.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 82.0 420.0 Td (2. Setup) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 82.0 401.1 Td (We train a two-layer network with 128 hidden units on 50,000 training examples, and keep 10,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 82.0 386.1 Td (examples for validation. We use mini-batch stochastic gradient descent with a batch size of 64, which) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 82.0 371.2 Td (gives 782 steps per epoch. Each run lasts at most 100 epochs. A run counts as converged when the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 82.0 356.2 Td (validation loss changes by less than 0.001 for five epochs in a row. Every setting is run with three) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 82.0 341.2 Td (random seeds and we report the mean.) Tj ET
